<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lucius Aemilius Paullus Macedonicus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 229–160 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a> · Also known as Aemilius Paullus, Lucius Aemilius Paullus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lucius Aemilius Paullus Macedonicus was a Roman general who defeated King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perseus-of-macedon">Perseus of Macedon</a> at Pydna in 168 BCE, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-macedonian-war">Third Macedonian War</a> and the Antigonid monarchy. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> then divided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a> into four republics. In 167 BCE, on the Senate's orders, he punished <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a> for supporting Perseus: seventy towns were plundered and about 150,000 people enslaved.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lucius-aemilius-paullus-macedonicus.jpg" alt="Lucius Aemilius Paullus Macedonicus" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lucius_Aemilius_Paullus_Macedonicus.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
